WEBVTT

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:08.070
This girl's weird.

00:00:08.070 --> 00:00:10.990
It's not winter, so what are 
you wearing a scarf for?

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:12.620
That is weird.

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:14.460
Maybe she's hiding something?

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:16.400
Let's take it off and see!

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:19.050
Stop it, you guys!

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:28.260
Leave my big sister alone!

00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:29.590
Kuro-chan.

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:34.400
Th-Thank you.

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:35.730
No problem.

00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:38.130
I'll always save you.

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:39.850
Kuro-chan...

00:00:40.430 --> 00:00:43.350
I'm here for you no matter what.

00:00:55.580 --> 00:00:58.280
<i>The points they took from Kuro-chan...</i>

00:00:58.650 --> 00:01:02.790
<i>I'm going to get them 
back, no matter what!</i>

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:06.910
R-Riichi.

00:01:09.780 --> 00:01:12.910
It's A Block's second round match.

00:01:12.910 --> 00:01:15.750
Here in the first half of the 
second players' match,

00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:18.120
Matsumi Yuu, from the current 
last place Achiga Girls',

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:19.470
has declared the first riichi.

00:01:27.640 --> 00:01:30.120
<i>Until now, Kuro-chan has always saved me,</i>

00:01:30.630 --> 00:01:34.550
<i>but today, I'm going to be 
the one who does the work!</i>

00:03:05.910 --> 00:03:08.700
<b>Round 6: 
Recovery</b>

00:03:13.590 --> 00:03:16.590
<i>No reaction to the 2 of circles.</i>

00:03:17.210 --> 00:03:19.930
<i>I guess I'll observe for now.</i>

00:03:23.740 --> 00:03:27.060
Yuck, I seriously have no safe tiles.

00:03:27.710 --> 00:03:30.430
I guess I'll take the challenge.

00:03:32.130 --> 00:03:32.780
Oh...

00:03:32.780 --> 00:03:34.240
Ron.

00:03:34.240 --> 00:03:37.150
Um... 3,200!

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:38.570
Are you serious?

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:39.830
Here you go.

00:03:41.160 --> 00:03:45.110
<i>Does this support 
Funakubo-senpai's data?</i>

00:03:51.860 --> 00:03:53.300
Hiroko?

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:55.170
Can you show me that thing again?

00:03:55.700 --> 00:03:56.780
Sure.

00:04:00.030 --> 00:04:02.720
This is a standard set of five 
East-South matches.

00:04:03.870 --> 00:04:06.390
This is Matsumi Yuu-chan.

00:04:07.510 --> 00:04:10.580
It's pretty clearly skewed 
towards characters and red dragons.

00:04:10.580 --> 00:04:12.920
I don't know if this is just 
a coincidence or what.

00:04:12.920 --> 00:04:14.940
You can see that from her play style.

00:04:16.230 --> 00:04:18.030
She'll throw away white and green dragons,

00:04:18.030 --> 00:04:20.630
but hold on to red dragons,
 even if she only has one.

00:04:20.630 --> 00:04:24.190
Plus, a lot of the time, she ends 
up getting more of them later.

00:04:24.190 --> 00:04:25.700
If an unconnected tile is a character,

00:04:25.700 --> 00:04:27.490
she usually doesn't discard it, either.

00:04:27.730 --> 00:04:30.230
That sort of play style means 
character and red dragon tiles

00:04:30.230 --> 00:04:32.750
come to her more readily.

00:04:33.170 --> 00:04:34.710
If she plays like that, it means...

00:04:37.320 --> 00:04:39.800
<i>Please come to me, warm-colored tiles...</i>

00:04:41.360 --> 00:04:42.510
<i>Warm-colored...</i>

00:04:44.560 --> 00:04:45.870
<i>More warm tiles... please!</i>

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:56.050
<i>So many warm tiles!</i>

00:04:57.830 --> 00:05:00.140
This hand isn't going anywhere.

00:05:02.740 --> 00:05:03.440
Pon!

00:05:06.130 --> 00:05:07.460
<i>Tenpai.</i>

00:05:09.190 --> 00:05:11.710
<i>She called the red dragon and 
discarded a character tile.</i>

00:05:11.710 --> 00:05:13.590
<i>Could you be any more obvious?</i>

00:05:14.540 --> 00:05:16.000
Sixth turn

00:05:19.690 --> 00:05:21.230
<i>I got a good one!</i>

00:05:21.230 --> 00:05:23.250
<i>But maybe it's too late...</i>

00:05:25.700 --> 00:05:26.590
Pon!

00:05:33.700 --> 00:05:36.710
<i>I guess that means Senriyama 
hasn't given up on this game yet,</i>

00:05:37.460 --> 00:05:40.550
<i>and now I got this dangerous tile...</i>

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:45.690
<i>I'm out!</i>

00:05:54.930 --> 00:05:56.770
<i>This tile isn't warm at all,</i>

00:05:57.280 --> 00:06:00.250
<i>but we're so far behind...</i>

00:06:02.750 --> 00:06:03.970
<i>I have to do it!</i>

00:06:04.490 --> 00:06:05.170
Ron!

00:06:06.930 --> 00:06:08.630
3,900.

00:06:09.400 --> 00:06:10.510
Yes.

00:06:13.130 --> 00:06:15.350
<i>A bamboo and circle kuitan...</i>

00:06:13.130 --> 00:06:15.350
[Kuitan - An open tanyao, a hand that lacks terminals or honors made by "eating" discards ]

00:06:16.580 --> 00:06:20.880
<i>Has she figured out my style?</i>

00:06:22.020 --> 00:06:24.490
<i>If you know that there's an imbalance,</i>

00:06:24.490 --> 00:06:26.290
<i>you've just got to set up your game</i>

00:06:26.290 --> 00:06:27.620
<i>with that in mind.</i>

00:06:29.570 --> 00:06:33.950
East Hand 3

00:06:33.310 --> 00:06:35.260
So far in this second players' match,

00:06:35.260 --> 00:06:37.680
Achiga won the first 
game for 3,200 points,

00:06:37.680 --> 00:06:40.000
followed by a 3,900 
point win by Senriyama.

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:41.210
Now it's the third East hand.

00:06:41.660 --> 00:06:43.940
Compared to Onjouji Toki's 
four hand winning streak

00:06:43.940 --> 00:06:45.760
to start the first players' match,

00:06:45.760 --> 00:06:48.590
you could say that it's 
a rather mild start.

00:06:48.590 --> 00:06:51.180
Hmm, well, I don't really know yet.

00:06:53.130 --> 00:06:55.930
The first year from 
Senriyama, Nijou Izumi:

00:06:55.930 --> 00:06:58.930
her data shows her performance 
to be very stable.

00:06:59.810 --> 00:07:02.160
<i>She protects most of the lead 
that Onjouji creates</i>

00:07:02.160 --> 00:07:04.060
<i>and hands it over to the third player.</i>

00:07:04.060 --> 00:07:07.990
I suppose she didn't become a 
regular as a first year for nothing.

00:07:08.820 --> 00:07:09.870
Onee-chan...

00:07:09.870 --> 00:07:11.240
Yuu-san, good luck!

00:07:13.660 --> 00:07:15.540
<i>I'm almost in tenpai.</i>

00:07:15.540 --> 00:07:16.230
Tsumo!

00:07:18.640 --> 00:07:20.870
1,300. 2,600.

00:07:26.380 --> 00:07:30.090
<i>I knew the bamboo and 
circle hand was coming.</i>

00:07:30.530 --> 00:07:32.080
With her second consecutive win,

00:07:32.080 --> 00:07:34.550
Senriyama's Nijou has just 
increased their lead.

00:07:35.100 --> 00:07:36.060
They know!

00:07:36.060 --> 00:07:36.950
Huh?

00:07:36.950 --> 00:07:38.760
What do you mean?

00:07:38.760 --> 00:07:41.680
Looks like Senriyama already figured out

00:07:41.680 --> 00:07:43.220
Yuu-san's playing style.

00:07:43.900 --> 00:07:45.650
It doesn't just "look like it."

00:07:46.430 --> 00:07:49.290
I'm 100% certain that they know.

00:07:50.000 --> 00:07:52.920
I wouldn't expect anything 
less from a top-class school

00:07:52.920 --> 00:07:54.410
like Senriyama.

00:07:55.560 --> 00:07:57.210
<i>What should I do?</i>

00:07:57.210 --> 00:07:59.710
<i>Remember.... what did I used to do?</i>

00:08:01.210 --> 00:08:04.840
<i>What did I do when I won against</i>

00:08:04.840 --> 00:08:08.420
<i>the players in our club 
who knew me even better?</i>

00:08:17.600 --> 00:08:18.870
<i>I'll try!</i>

00:08:18.390 --> 00:08:20.140
East Hand 4

00:08:18.390 --> 00:08:20.140
Ninth turn

00:08:21.140 --> 00:08:23.140
East (Dealer)
Achiga Girls' Academy (Nara)
3rd year - Second player
Matsumi Yuu

00:08:26.510 --> 00:08:29.360
<i>She dropped a pair of red dragons 
with those discards...</i>

00:08:29.360 --> 00:08:30.730
<i>I guess she went from</i>

00:08:30.730 --> 00:08:33.590
<i>a character honitsu to a chinitsu to try 
and make a dent into the point gap.</i>

00:08:30.730 --> 00:08:33.590
[Honitsu - half flush including one suit and honors; 
Chinitsu - full flush with only one suit]

00:08:34.380 --> 00:08:36.530
<i>Then she'll be in tenpai soon.</i>

00:08:36.530 --> 00:08:37.810
<i>I guess I'll stay out of this one.</i>

00:09:07.480 --> 00:09:09.850
<i>So I guess Senriyama's getting out</i>

00:09:09.850 --> 00:09:11.690
<i>because they predict Achiga's closed chinitsu.</i>

00:09:19.120 --> 00:09:22.250
<i>There's no more matching 
safe tiles, but let's see.</i>

00:09:26.730 --> 00:09:27.710
<i>Suji.</i>

00:09:26.730 --> 00:09:27.710
[Suji - Tiles that are 3 apart, 
completing a sequence; ex: 3/6/9]

00:09:32.810 --> 00:09:34.170
<i>This is bad.</i>

00:09:34.170 --> 00:09:35.240
Ron.

00:09:35.240 --> 00:09:37.090
Tanyao, sanshoku, one dora.

00:09:35.240 --> 00:09:37.090
[Sanshoku - 3 suit/color (sequence or triplets)]

00:09:37.780 --> 00:09:39.470
That's 12,000.

00:09:42.140 --> 00:09:43.850
<i>Her hand isn't one color!</i>

00:09:44.490 --> 00:09:46.140
<i>It does happen that I think</i>

00:09:46.140 --> 00:09:49.360
<i>someone's hand is all 
one color, when it isn't,</i>

00:09:50.230 --> 00:09:51.610
<i>but this is...</i>

00:09:51.610 --> 00:09:52.940
What's going on?

00:09:53.280 --> 00:09:54.730
Huh?

00:09:59.960 --> 00:10:01.530
It's not red dragons and characters,

00:10:03.730 --> 00:10:05.330
but tiles with red!

00:10:09.020 --> 00:10:12.030
Yikes, so it looks like 
the profile was wrong.

00:10:12.030 --> 00:10:14.540
Make sure to tell her after the
 first half of the match is over.

00:10:14.540 --> 00:10:16.910
No, this is a little...

00:10:16.910 --> 00:10:17.800
A little what?

00:10:18.510 --> 00:10:19.300
Riichi!

00:10:20.190 --> 00:10:22.650
There might not be a simple 
solution for this...

00:10:28.690 --> 00:10:30.560
<i>I guess I'll rely on the suji.</i>

00:10:33.650 --> 00:10:34.620
Ron.

00:10:35.610 --> 00:10:37.030
Riichi only.

00:10:37.030 --> 00:10:39.450
That's 2,700.

00:10:47.250 --> 00:10:49.700
<i>This game's become a pain in the neck.</i>

00:10:56.400 --> 00:10:58.550
The second players' match is over!

00:10:58.550 --> 00:11:00.300
We finish with a win by

00:11:00.300 --> 00:11:02.050
Senriyama's Nijou Izumi in the last hand.

00:11:04.460 --> 00:11:06.480
Thank you for the game.

00:11:06.480 --> 00:11:07.740
Thanks!

00:11:07.740 --> 00:11:08.930
Thank you.

00:11:08.930 --> 00:11:10.310
Later.

00:11:24.000 --> 00:11:25.800
<i>She got me.</i>

00:11:26.920 --> 00:11:30.910
None of the schools have changed positions 
after the second players' match.

00:11:30.910 --> 00:11:34.800
Senriyama, the leader, increases 
their lead over second place,

00:11:34.800 --> 00:11:36.500
while last place Achiga slightly closes

00:11:36.500 --> 00:11:38.460
the deficit with the other schools.

00:11:38.460 --> 00:11:40.470
<b>Achiga Girls'</b>

00:11:38.460 --> 00:11:41.190
We will now be moving on to 
the third players' match!

00:11:54.450 --> 00:11:56.570
I'm back.

00:11:56.920 --> 00:11:58.460
Welcome back, Yuu-nee.

00:11:58.460 --> 00:11:59.780
Welcome back.

00:11:59.780 --> 00:12:01.750
Good job!

00:12:01.750 --> 00:12:03.190
Well done!

00:12:05.590 --> 00:12:07.610
Thank you, onee-chan!

00:12:07.610 --> 00:12:09.130
I'm sorry, Kuro-chan.

00:12:09.130 --> 00:12:11.360
I only got a few of your points back.

00:12:11.360 --> 00:12:12.700
That doesn't matter!

00:12:12.700 --> 00:12:14.270
You came out on top this match!

00:12:14.270 --> 00:12:16.200
I simply lost us too many points!

00:12:16.200 --> 00:12:17.960
That's true.

00:12:18.980 --> 00:12:21.210
But then again, you were playing

00:12:21.210 --> 00:12:23.010
a school that's a regular at the nationals.

00:12:23.380 --> 00:12:26.040
This was more or less expected.

00:12:26.040 --> 00:12:30.060
Now all we've got to do 
is get those points back!

00:12:30.640 --> 00:12:31.480
I guess.

00:12:33.400 --> 00:12:34.690
You guys...

00:12:34.690 --> 00:12:36.650
Then let's do it!

00:12:59.620 --> 00:13:03.030
The third players' match 
will be starting shortly.

00:13:01.970 --> 00:13:04.970
Second round match - Second game 
 Third players' match starts in 5 minutes

00:13:03.030 --> 00:13:05.270
We ask that the each school's 
representative please come

00:13:04.970 --> 00:13:07.970
<b>Senriyama Girls'</b>

00:13:05.270 --> 00:13:07.040
to the tournament hall at this time.

00:13:07.040 --> 00:13:07.970
All right!

00:13:08.410 --> 00:13:10.490
I guess I'm off.

00:13:12.360 --> 00:13:14.270
Are you planning on going like that?

00:13:14.270 --> 00:13:15.310
Is it wrong?

00:13:15.700 --> 00:13:17.080
Hurry up.

00:13:17.080 --> 00:13:18.150
Yes, yes.

00:13:19.110 --> 00:13:20.800
I joined under the condition

00:13:20.800 --> 00:13:23.320
that I don't have to 
wear a skirt at school.

00:13:23.320 --> 00:13:26.320
Having to wear a skirt in matches 
makes me feel like I got conned.

00:13:26.320 --> 00:13:29.210
I feel like this exchange happens 
pretty much every time.

00:13:29.210 --> 00:13:30.660
It's just for two hours.

00:13:31.060 --> 00:13:33.020
In my middle school we didn't have a uniform

00:13:33.020 --> 00:13:36.120
so I didn't have any contact with 
this frilly stuff until high school!

00:13:36.120 --> 00:13:37.790
Stop your whining.

00:13:40.200 --> 00:13:43.210
Damn it, it feels so airy...

00:13:43.190 --> 00:13:44.920
Senriyama Girls' (North Osaka)
3rd year - Third player
Eguchi Sera

00:13:45.750 --> 00:13:47.480
It suits you well, you know.

00:13:47.480 --> 00:13:48.710
You look cute!

00:13:48.710 --> 00:13:50.540
Fair feathers make fair fowls, is it?

00:13:50.540 --> 00:13:51.660
Shut up.

00:13:52.310 --> 00:13:54.090
I'm back.

00:13:54.090 --> 00:13:54.890
Welcome back.

00:13:56.130 --> 00:13:58.270
Wow! You're in maiden mode.

00:14:00.730 --> 00:14:02.420
I'm going now.

00:14:03.820 --> 00:14:05.100
She ran away.

00:14:05.100 --> 00:14:07.940
She's running away from 
us, into the public eye.

00:14:11.240 --> 00:14:12.700
Sera!

00:14:12.700 --> 00:14:13.910
Could we just have a quick word?

00:14:13.910 --> 00:14:15.660
Over here, please!

00:14:15.660 --> 00:14:18.580
How do you feel about your game?

00:14:18.580 --> 00:14:21.340
How would you say you're 
feeling today, Sera?

00:14:30.070 --> 00:14:32.200
As we approach the second match, 
the top ranked Senriyama

00:14:32.200 --> 00:14:33.810
has firmly secured their lead.

00:14:32.300 --> 00:14:33.810
Achiga Girls' (Nara)
 1st Year - Third Player
Atarashi Ako

00:14:33.810 --> 00:14:36.770
but the gaps between the
 other schools have shrunk,

00:14:36.770 --> 00:14:39.690
meaning that it's still 
very much undecided

00:14:38.330 --> 00:14:40.810
Koshigaya Girls' (Saitama)
1st Year - Third Player
Mizumura Shiori

00:14:39.690 --> 00:14:42.020
who will move on 
to the semi-finals.

00:14:42.020 --> 00:14:44.820
The third players' match 
will begin momentarily.

00:14:42.310 --> 00:14:44.820
Kentani High School (Hyougo)
3rd Year - Third Player
Furuzuka Kozue

00:14:56.750 --> 00:14:58.540
Did you already decide places?

00:15:00.220 --> 00:15:01.170
Go ahead.

00:15:01.170 --> 00:15:02.460
Don't mind if I do.

00:15:03.770 --> 00:15:06.960
North

00:15:05.860 --> 00:15:06.960
East

00:15:09.260 --> 00:15:11.090
Good luck, guys.

00:15:11.520 --> 00:15:12.690
Same.

00:15:12.690 --> 00:15:14.430
Thank you all for this game.

00:15:16.060 --> 00:15:17.870
Good luck.

00:15:17.870 --> 00:15:19.270
Go easy on me.

00:15:20.240 --> 00:15:22.630
<i>She has just as much 
needless energy as Shizu,</i>

00:15:22.630 --> 00:15:25.180
<i>but just last year,
 she was a second year</i>

00:15:25.180 --> 00:15:28.780
<i>playing as Senriyama's ace.</i>

00:15:29.270 --> 00:15:31.800
<i>That girl is the president 
of Kentani's club.</i>

00:15:31.800 --> 00:15:35.780
<i>If I let my guard down, 
I'll be torn to shreds.</i>

00:15:36.230 --> 00:15:39.550
<i>I'll start by winning one hand.</i>

00:15:48.660 --> 00:15:50.150
Nozomi-chan.

00:15:50.150 --> 00:15:52.550
Ako-chan's game is about to start.

00:15:52.550 --> 00:15:54.260
I'll finish up here.

00:15:54.260 --> 00:15:55.510
Thank you.

00:15:59.810 --> 00:16:00.890
Come on, dora!

00:16:00.890 --> 00:16:01.770
A-chan!

00:16:01.770 --> 00:16:03.340
Ako-chan, fight!

00:16:04.470 --> 00:16:06.280
Go, go, Ako-chan!

00:16:06.280 --> 00:16:07.590
Go get 'em!

00:16:07.590 --> 00:16:08.780
Ako-chan!

00:16:09.540 --> 00:16:11.950
Good luck, Ako-senpai!

00:16:13.820 --> 00:16:15.810
<i>Good luck, Ako.</i>

00:16:16.430 --> 00:16:18.490
Excuse me!

00:16:21.700 --> 00:16:23.910
Hatsuse-chan, is that you?

00:16:24.770 --> 00:16:26.300
I'm sorry to just barge in,

00:16:26.300 --> 00:16:29.050
but has Ako's match already started?

00:16:29.110 --> 00:16:32.760
Third Match

00:16:29.110 --> 00:16:32.760
East Hand 1
Dealer: Mizumura Shiori

00:16:40.770 --> 00:16:41.890
Chi!

00:16:46.440 --> 00:16:47.270
Pon!

00:16:52.010 --> 00:16:52.860
Ron.

00:16:54.920 --> 00:16:56.280
7,700.

00:16:56.810 --> 00:16:58.220
That was fast.

00:16:58.220 --> 00:16:59.180
Here you go.

00:17:00.530 --> 00:17:03.790
Achiga gets the first win of 
the third players' match.

00:17:04.280 --> 00:17:08.160
With a direct hit on Kentani, 
they get out of last place.

00:17:08.160 --> 00:17:10.870
She's Achiga's best player,

00:17:10.870 --> 00:17:12.880
though she doesn't get as much attention

00:17:12.880 --> 00:17:14.300
because the upperclassmen are so special.

00:17:14.670 --> 00:17:17.130
If that girl transferred to Senriyama,

00:17:17.130 --> 00:17:19.890
she'd probably be one of 
the top ten first years.

00:17:19.890 --> 00:17:21.650
You're looking down on her...

00:17:21.650 --> 00:17:24.060
Her calling sense is especially good.

00:17:24.060 --> 00:17:27.660
I like how she accelerates 
when she calls and attacks.

00:17:30.030 --> 00:17:30.900
Tsumo!

00:17:30.900 --> 00:17:32.210
1,000. 2,000.

00:17:33.690 --> 00:17:35.030
Oh, Ako!

00:17:35.030 --> 00:17:36.390
Crap!

00:17:36.390 --> 00:17:37.820
Don't you lose this, Shiori!

00:17:37.820 --> 00:17:39.450
Not Achiga again!

00:17:39.450 --> 00:17:40.620
Senpai.

00:17:40.620 --> 00:17:41.910
Oh, jeez!

00:17:41.910 --> 00:17:46.750
As if Senriyama's Sera wasn't enough 
trouble already for Kozue-chan!

00:17:47.210 --> 00:17:49.280
Achiga Girls' Academy's 
Atarashi Ako has now

00:17:49.280 --> 00:17:50.620
won two hands in a row.

00:17:50.620 --> 00:17:52.250
She calls well!

00:17:52.650 --> 00:17:55.570
They're playing here for the 
first time in ten years,

00:17:55.570 --> 00:17:59.730
but Atarashi is the only regular 
player on Achiga's team

00:17:59.730 --> 00:18:02.220
who's played in an official 
tournament in middle school.

00:18:02.220 --> 00:18:03.580
Is that so?

00:18:03.580 --> 00:18:04.680
That's right.

00:18:04.680 --> 00:18:07.360
Her best result was top 16 in her

00:18:07.360 --> 00:18:09.520
prefecture in an individual tournament.

00:18:09.520 --> 00:18:12.840
Then I guess she's improved
 since she started high school?

00:18:12.840 --> 00:18:15.200
I think she's always had the potential,

00:18:15.200 --> 00:18:16.810
but it's not just that.

00:18:16.780 --> 00:18:20.990
Akado Harue
Made it to the semi-finals in the 61st 
National High School Mahjong Tournament
Last year she went to the play-offs 
with the Hakata Evergreens
Coach of the Achiga Girls' 
Academy Mahjong Club

00:18:16.810 --> 00:18:18.550
She's put in a lot of hard work,

00:18:18.550 --> 00:18:20.990
and she's had some 
excellent guidance of late.

00:18:21.680 --> 00:18:24.030
You might be right about that.

00:18:24.690 --> 00:18:26.450
Ako's amazing.

00:18:26.450 --> 00:18:27.990
She's playing at a national level,

00:18:27.990 --> 00:18:29.860
but she doesn't seem affected.

00:18:29.860 --> 00:18:31.340
Here you go.

00:18:31.340 --> 00:18:32.830
Oh, thank you.

00:18:32.830 --> 00:18:34.460
You don't have your club today?

00:18:34.460 --> 00:18:38.760
Yes, during summer break we 
meet three times a week.

00:18:38.760 --> 00:18:40.780
Our school is supposed to 
be a prep school, after all.

00:18:40.780 --> 00:18:41.690
That's true.

00:18:41.690 --> 00:18:44.430
Getting into Bansei is tough.

00:18:45.250 --> 00:18:47.520
Senriyama and Kentani, huh?

00:18:49.000 --> 00:18:52.260
If Wabuka and we were there, 
this would be just like the

00:18:52.260 --> 00:18:54.520
semi-finals of last fall's Kinki Tournament.

00:18:54.520 --> 00:18:56.030
You remembered.

00:18:56.030 --> 00:19:00.560
Yes. Ako usually went straight 
home after we were done,

00:19:00.560 --> 00:19:03.690
but that day she stuck around, 
and we watched it together

00:19:03.690 --> 00:19:05.300
in the club room at Ada Middle School.

00:19:05.300 --> 00:19:07.450
Thinking back, she was already

00:19:07.450 --> 00:19:09.540
playing with Achiga's mahjong club

00:19:09.540 --> 00:19:11.500
to prepare for the nationals.

00:19:11.880 --> 00:19:13.030
I guess so.

00:19:13.030 --> 00:19:15.550
But they weren't an official club yet

00:19:15.550 --> 00:19:18.960
and Harue didn't come until that winter.

00:19:18.960 --> 00:19:20.260
Wow.

00:19:20.570 --> 00:19:23.950
Back then, we were sitting around 
watching it together on TV,

00:19:23.950 --> 00:19:26.370
and now Ako is there,

00:19:26.370 --> 00:19:28.520
playing against all these great players.

00:19:28.520 --> 00:19:30.810
I envy her, to be honest.

00:19:31.250 --> 00:19:33.890
But Hatsuse-chan, I bet 
you're thinking that

00:19:33.890 --> 00:19:35.260
you'll be there next year, right?

00:19:36.610 --> 00:19:38.280
Yes, of course!

00:19:40.740 --> 00:19:43.370
<i>I guess I'm in tenpai...</i>

00:19:47.580 --> 00:19:50.720
<i>She tends to go for tanyao,</i>

00:19:50.720 --> 00:19:52.790
<i>but I'd like some points, too.</i>

00:19:54.880 --> 00:19:55.630
Ron!

00:19:56.100 --> 00:19:57.340
3,900!

00:19:57.340 --> 00:19:58.340
No...

00:19:58.930 --> 00:20:00.750
Atarashi Ako from Achiga Girls',

00:20:00.750 --> 00:20:02.050
gets her third consecutive win!

00:20:02.050 --> 00:20:04.380
Now she's the dealer.

00:20:03.340 --> 00:20:07.140
East Hand 4

00:20:10.970 --> 00:20:12.810
<i>She's running fast.</i>

00:20:17.090 --> 00:20:20.190
<i>Depending on the rules, 
that might be fine...</i>

00:20:23.610 --> 00:20:26.570
Sixth Turn

00:20:29.580 --> 00:20:33.710
<i>but this team match is about 
who's got the most at the end.</i>

00:20:35.810 --> 00:20:36.790
Riichi.

00:20:37.470 --> 00:20:38.210
Chi.

00:20:42.890 --> 00:20:44.590
<i>She's the dealer now, too.</i>

00:20:45.150 --> 00:20:46.250
<i>I'm out.</i>

00:20:47.490 --> 00:20:49.220
<i>I can't play into another hand.</i>

00:20:51.850 --> 00:20:53.850
<i>Rather than three 3,900 point hands...</i>

00:20:54.850 --> 00:20:55.800
Tsumo!

00:20:57.850 --> 00:20:59.360
3,000. 6,000.

00:21:02.430 --> 00:21:05.360
<i>I prefer winning 12,000 point hands.</i>

00:21:06.340 --> 00:21:08.540
<i>I should've figured it 
wouldn't be that easy.</i>

00:21:09.390 --> 00:21:10.410
<i>But...</i>

00:21:11.770 --> 00:21:13.540
<i>In this third players' match...</i>

00:21:13.540 --> 00:21:15.710
<i>I'm going to take more points!</i>

00:21:34.960 --> 00:21:37.190
The third players' match is over!

00:21:38.150 --> 00:21:41.550
This match became a fight 
between Senriyama and Achiga,

00:21:41.550 --> 00:21:43.070
exchanging the lead with each other.

00:21:43.590 --> 00:21:45.610
In the end, Senriyama has boosted

00:21:44.340 --> 00:21:47.570
Senriyama Girls' (North Osaka)
3rd year - Third Player
Eguchi Sera

00:21:45.610 --> 00:21:47.210
their lead even more.

00:21:47.950 --> 00:21:51.040
The fight for second place is 
getting more and more ferocious.

00:21:48.320 --> 00:21:51.580
Achiga Girls' (Nara)
1st year - Third player
Atarashi Ako

00:21:51.040 --> 00:21:52.860
Thanks to their excellent performance,

00:21:52.330 --> 00:21:55.580
Koshigaya Girls' (Saitama)
1st year - Third player
Mizumura Shiori

00:21:52.860 --> 00:21:55.140
Achiga has risen from 
last to second place.

00:21:55.580 --> 00:21:57.550
Faring not so well, Koshigaya

00:21:56.330 --> 00:21:59.580
Kentani High School (Hyougo)
3rd Year - Third Player
Furuzuka Kozue

00:21:57.550 --> 00:21:59.590
has fallen from second to last place.

00:21:59.590 --> 00:22:02.590
Kentani had gone under early, 
but regained their composure

00:22:02.590 --> 00:22:04.270
and maintained their 
position in third place.

00:22:04.700 --> 00:22:07.320
However, all three schools 
are not far apart.

00:22:12.910 --> 00:22:13.770
All right!

00:22:16.700 --> 00:22:18.860
It's up to you now, Arata-san!

00:22:18.860 --> 00:22:20.740
Go get 'em, Arata-chan!

00:22:20.740 --> 00:22:22.190
Good luck!

00:22:22.930 --> 00:22:24.690
We're counting on you, Arata.

00:22:42.430 --> 00:22:43.600
I'm off.

00:24:04.920 --> 00:24:19.930
<b>Conviction</b>

00:24:06.130 --> 00:24:07.590
What is that thing called again?

00:24:07.590 --> 00:24:10.550
You wedge it in when you're 
tightening a bolt with a nut

00:24:10.550 --> 00:24:13.390
and it's kind of round and 
looks like the 1 of circles...

00:24:13.390 --> 00:24:14.410
You mean a washer?

00:24:14.410 --> 00:24:15.720
Yeah, that's it! A washer!

00:24:15.720 --> 00:24:16.640
Why do you even 
know what that is,

00:24:16.640 --> 00:24:18.100
and what do you need it for?!
